        "original_id": "fd9d69f1-a207-56f5-a436-040b40fcdbff",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Larry Gagosian, Steve Dildarian\n- Companies: Gagosian Gallery, HBO\n- Products: The Life & Times of Tim\n- Places: New York City, Nathaniel L. McCready House\n- Roles: art dealer, advertising copywriter, creator, writer, producer, voice actor\n\nFacts:\n- Larry Gagosian was born on April 19, 1945, and he is an Armenian American art dealer.\n- Larry Gagosian owns the Gagosian Gallery chain of art galleries.\n- Steve Dildarian was born on November 3, 1969, and he is an American former advertising copywriter.\n- Steve Dildarian created The Life & Times of Tim for HBO and served as its writer, producer, and the voice of Tim from 2008 to 2012.\n- The Life & Times of Tim is about Tim, a hapless man in his mid-20s who lives in New York City with his girlfriend Amy.\n- In 2011, Larry Gagosian purchased the Nathaniel L. McCready House and demolished the mansion's interior.",
